  "solution": {
    "text": "<img alt=\"\" height=\"183\" src=\"assets\\st0236_56dd28490afd.jpg\" width=\"114\" /><br /><br /><math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> group has electron withdrawing nature<br /><br /><math><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> group has electron releasing nature so in para positions <math><munder accentunder=\"false\"><mo>→</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></math> and <math><munder accentunder=\"false\"><mo>→</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></math> will simply add up to give the maximum value of resultant dipole moment of the molecule <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></math> ."
